        "label": "Parts of the apparatus",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Parts",
        "lines": [
          "A pair of salivary glands lies on either side",
          "of the crop.",
          "Each gland has two lobes, and each lobe has",
          "many lobules called acini.",
          "Each acinus is made of secretory cells called",
          "zymogen cells.",
          "A pair of salivary receptacles stores the",
          "saliva."
        ],
        "why": "The drawing shows glands and receptacles as separate shapes, so naming them first tells the examiner which shape in the figure is which before the ducts are traced.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing one gland. There is a PAIR of glands and a PAIR of receptacles, one set on each side of the crop.",
          "Calling the receptacle a gland. The gland makes the saliva; the receptacle only stores it."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Two on each side: a lobed gland that makes saliva and a plain sac that stores it.",
        "margin_note": "Four short lines: pair of glands, two lobes, acini of zymogen cells, pair of receptacles."
